comments.body:
I'm not able to produce this with the approach outlined above reliably. But I can make the tab-switch become sluggish by doing what @reporter suggested at the beginning. The more tabs I have the worse it gets. Can you try this:

1. test.kdl:
```kdl
layout {
    default_tab_template {
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="zellij:tab-bar"
        }
        children
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="zellij:status-bar"
        }
    }
    tab name="1" focus=true {
      pane command="sh" {
          args "-c" "echo 'Pane 1 content'; cat"
      }
    }
    tab name="2" {
      pane command="sh" {
          args "-c" "echo 'Pane 2 content'; cat"
      }
    }
    tab name="3" {
      pane command="sh" {
          args "-c" "echo 'Pane 3 content'; cat"
      }
    }
    tab name="4" {
      pane command="sh" {
          args "-c" "echo 'Pane 4 content'; cat"
      }
    }
    tab name="5" {
      pane command="sh" {
          args "-c" "echo 'Pane 5 content'; cat"
      }
    }
}
```
2. run `zellij --config-dir /tmp/zellij-clean -n test.kdl -s test`
2. keep holding Alt+right-arrow for a few seconds (~5)

Observations:
- The pane content switches quickly, but the tabs keep transitioning for much longer.
- When I invoke the session-manager (`C-o w`) while the tabs are still transitioning, the session-manager is blocked (can't select any entry)
